    description: "WI-kudir (PR #689) fixed extension-declared Swift members (incl. extension subscripts) to attribute to their type. But struct-BODY subscripts were ALREADY correctly named (e.g. 'JSON.subscript(key:)') before that fix, yet WI-kudir's original evidence claimed all 6 SwiftyJSON subscripts had 0 contains + 0 incoming. The Swift analyzer emits NO contains edges directly — containment is built by a downstream core pass from symbol names. UNVERIFIED (low-confidence WATCH): whether the downstream containment builder attaches a correctly-named 'Type.subscript(key:)' node under its type, or whether the '(key:)'/'(index:)' parenthesized name-suffix format breaks its parent-name extraction. Action: run the full hypergumbo pipeline on SwiftyJSON post-#689 and check contains/incoming on the struct-body subscripts; if still 0, the defect is in the core containment builder for subscript-kind or the parenthesized-name parse, not the Swift analyzer."  # 21bc
    fields: {}  # 21bc
- op: discuss  # c00e
  at: '2026-07-16T20:06:31Z'  # c00e
  by: agent  # c00e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c00e
  clock: 2  # c00e
  nonce: c00e  # c00e
  message: "VERIFIED REAL (2026-07-16, owner asked to verify before committing). Ran the full pipeline on a struct-body-subscript fixture (correctly-named JSON.subscript(key:) / JSON.subscript(index:), NOT extension-declared — so distinct from what WI-kudir/#689 already fixed). Result: the JSON struct's contains edges cover [JSON.raw (field), JSON.merge (method)] but NOT the subscripts — both subscripts have 0 contains AND 0 incoming. So it IS a real gap, and NOT a Swift-analyzer issue: the LOCUS is the core containment linker. CONTAINABLE_KINDS (packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/containment.py:99-106) = {method, getter, setter, message, function, variable, field} — 'subscript' is absent, so subscript-kind members are never attached to their enclosing type. FIX (facet 1, contains): add 'subscript' to CONTAINABLE_KINDS — a one-liner (Infrastructure linker, not Swift). Note: the module docstring states contains is NOT traversed by the dead-code BFS, so this de-orphaning does not move the dead-code-maybe FP rate — its value is graph completeness (the flagship json[...] subscripts stop looking like orphaned/hollow members of the central type). FACET 2 (0 incoming): the j[\"key\"] subscript-CALL site does not resolve to the subscript node — a separate Swift-analyzer subscript-call-resolution gap (out of scope for the containment one-liner). Reframed from unverified-WATCH to confirmed; keep in Wave 5. Priority: the contains one-liner is trivial; the incoming-resolution facet is the larger, more valuable piece."  # c00e
- op: discuss  # 8838
