  clock: 3  # 8838
  nonce: '8838'  # 8838
  message: "Facet 1 (contains) SHIPPED in PR #695 (dev 5dcfad4927): added 'subscript' to CONTAINABLE_KINDS in linkers/containment.py, so correctly-named struct-body Swift subscripts (JSON.subscript(key:)) now attach to their enclosing type. Verified by co-located test test_containment_linker.py::test_swift_struct_body_subscript (parent-name extraction already handled the parenthesized (key:) suffix; only the kind gate blocked the edge). Graph-completeness only — the dead-code BFS does not traverse contains, so no dead-code FP-rate change.\n\nFacet 2 REMAINS OPEN (this item stays open, scoped to it): the json[\"key\"] subscript-CALL site still does not resolve to the subscript node (0 incoming) — a Swift-analyzer subscript-call-resolution gap, distinct from and larger than the containment one-liner."  # 8838
- op: discuss  # 9c5c
  at: '2026-11-01T22:22:24Z'  # 9c5c
  by: agent  # 9c5c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9c5c
  clock: 4  # 9c5c
  nonce: 9c5c  # 9c5c
  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/langs1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 9ae4abe13f (fx_fokag). Facet 1, the title's contains check, is done: JSON contains both JSON.subscript(key:) and JSON.subscript(index:) (PR #695). Facet 2 holds: j[\"name\"], j[3] and k[\"x\"] produce no edge, so both subscripts have 0 incoming. The mechanism has moved: 69b357ce47 (WI-dimad) now drops every subscript as a member access on purpose, so the fix is a positive binding to the receiver type's subscript, not a mis-emitted call. Side note: j.merge() on a parameter typed JSON also emitted no calls edge in this fixture. MECHANISM: subscript call sites are suppressed as member access (WI-dimad) and never bound to the receiver type's subscript symbol."  # 9c5c
